🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
Summary
We want (and should) support all of CSR, CSC, BSR and BSC using just SparseCsrTensorImpl.
We currently have a many-to-one relationship between dispatch keys and layouts.
  Layout layout() const {
    // NB: This method is not virtual and avoid dispatches for perf.
    if (is_sparse()) {
      return kSparse;
    } else if (is_sparse_csr()) {
      return kSparseCsr;
    } else if (is_mkldnn()) {
      return kMkldnn;
    } else {
      return kStrided;
    }
  }

Each of the "is_*" methods checks whether the TensorImpl has one of a certain set of dispatch keys.
We should be able to map from one dispatch key to multiple layouts.
Virtualizing layout for sparse Tensors
Layout TensorImpl::layout() const is not virtual for performance and we can't change that. Introducing a new field also has downsides (memory), so if we can we should avoid adding a new field.
Now, to sidestep very long discussions around performance and memory footprint this proposal aims to find a solution that is slower for users of sparse Tensors, but shouldn't interfere with existing applications.

Introduce virtual Layout TensorImpl::slow_layout const
SparseCsrTensorImpl overwrites slow_layout to return the correct layout (e.g. CSC or BSC) to yield Layout SparseCsrTensorImpl::slow_layout const
Layout TensorImpl::layout() const calls into slow_layout when needed.

The final version of Layout TensorImpl::layout const then should look like
  Layout layout() const {
    // NB: This method is not virtual and avoid dispatches for perf.
    if (is_sparse()) {
      return kSparse;
    } else if (is_sparse_csr()) {
      return slow_layout(); // This is new
    } else if (is_mkldnn()) {
      return kMkldnn;
    } else {
      return kStrided;
    }
  }

Further fallout
dispatchKeyToLayout will need to be modified to throw in cases where it's not possible to determine the relationship uniquely. This affects the constructors also via dispatchKeyToTensorOptions.
Callsites for dispatchKeyToLayout
legacy constructor - uses dispatchKeyToLayout to get layout of default dispatch key (which is CPU), so this won't have to change.
Callsites for dispatchKeyToTensorOptions
_validate_sparse_coo_tensor_args - can construct TensorOptions by other means or we extend dispatchKeyToLayout to accept a Layout in cases where it's necessary to disambiguate.
_validate_sparse_csr_tensor_args - same story as _validate_sparse_coo_tensor_args
Alternatives
We could introduce one dispatch key per Layout+Device combination like we're currently doing, but then we'll run out of dispatch keys, which we've just worked so hard to free up.
Additional context
No response
